-- title:
--   §8.1–§8.4 — the localized bound (8.3), Aₘ, Dₘ, 𝓕⁽ᵐ⁾, Ω_{n,t,m}, Ω(m, n, S, i)±, Ũⁿ(m), Ũ(m), X″(m) and Hⁿ(m)
-- statement:
--   The objects of the proof of Theorem 3.1 (§8). Fix the scheme $(\Delta_n,u_n,k_n)$, a function $\gamma\ge0$ on $E$ and an integer $m\ge0$.
--
--   1. **The localized bound (8.3)** with constant $C$, process $\Gamma$ and functions $\gamma,\widehat\gamma\ge0$: $\int_E(\gamma^r\wedge1)\,d\lambda<\infty$ and $\int_E(\widehat\gamma^{q}\wedge1)\,d\lambda<\infty$ ($q=2$ if $v\le\tfrac12$, $q=1/v$ otherwise); $|\delta|\le\Gamma\gamma$, $|\widehat\delta|\le\Gamma\widehat\gamma$; $\Gamma$ plays $\Gamma'$ in (2.2); and for all $\omega,t,z$, $\sigma_t\neq0$ and
--   $$|b_t|+|\sigma_t|+\frac1{|\sigma_t|}+|\widehat b_t|+|\widehat\sigma_t|+|\widehat\sigma'_t|+\Gamma_t+|Z_t|+|\overline Z_t|+\gamma(z)+\widehat\gamma(z)\le C.$$
--   2. $A_m=\{z:\gamma(z)\le1/m\}$ for $m\ge1$, and $A_0=E$. $D_m(\omega)$ is the set of times $s$ of the atoms $(s,z)$ of $\mu$ with $z\notin A_m$ (the big jumps).
--   3. $\mathcal G_m$ is the $\sigma$-field generated by the restriction of $\mu$ to $\mathbb R_+\times A_m^c$, and $\mathcal F^{(m)}_t=\mathcal F_t\vee\mathcal G_m$.
--   4. $\Omega_{n,t,m}$ is the event that any two distinct times $T\neq T'$ of $D_m$ satisfy $T>t$, or $T>3k_n\Delta_n$ and $|T-T'|>6k_n\Delta_n$.
--   5. For a random time $S$ and a random integer $i$,
--   $$\Omega(m,n,S,i)_+=\{(i-1)\Delta_n<S\le i\Delta_n,\ (S,S+(k_n+1)\Delta_n]\cap D_m=\varnothing\},$$
--   $$\Omega(m,n,S,i)_-=\{(i-1)\Delta_n<S\le i\Delta_n,\ (S-(k_n+2)\Delta_n,S)\cap D_m=\varnothing\}.$$
--   6. With $i(n,s)=\lceil s/\Delta_n\rceil$ (so $s\in((i-1)\Delta_n,i\Delta_n]$), the big-jump part of $U(F,k_n)$ and its limit are
--   $$\widetilde U^n(m)_t=\sum_{s\in D_m,\ s\le\Delta_n[t/\Delta_n]}F\big(\Delta^n_{i(n,s)}X,\widehat c(k_n)_{i(n,s)-k_n-1},\widehat c(k_n)_{i(n,s)}\big)1_{\{|\Delta^n_{i(n,s)}X|>u_n\}},$$
--   $$\widetilde U(m)_t=\sum_{s\in D_m,\ s\le t}F(\Delta X_s,c_{s-},c_s)\,1_{\{\Delta X_s\neq0\}}.$$
--   7. $X''(m)$ is the small-jump process of (8.5): $X''(m)_t=\int_0^t\int_{A_m}\delta(s,z)(\mu-\nu)(ds,dz)$ if $r>1$, and $X''(m)_t=\int_0^t\int_{A_m}\delta(s,z)\,\mu(ds,dz)$ (an a.s. absolutely convergent sum over the atoms) if $r\le1$.
--   8. $H^n(m)_t=\sum_{i=k_n+1}^{[t/\Delta_n]-k_n}|\Delta^n_iX''(m)|^r\big(1+\widehat c(k_n)_{i-k_n-1}+\widehat c(k_n)_i\big)$, without the constant factor $K$ of the page.
--
--   These are the objects of (8.4), Lemma 8.1, (8.27) and (8.29), the steps of the proof of Theorem 3.1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The printed (8.3) also bounds $|X_t|$. That term is omitted: together with $|b_t|\le C$ and $1/|\sigma_t|\le C$ for all $t\ge0$, $|X_t|\le C$ for all $t$ is impossible ($e^{aX_t}$, for large $a$, would be bounded with a drift bounded below by a positive constant), so it would make every statement under (8.3) vacuous; the localization of §8.1 delivers exactly the bounds kept. The enumeration $(T_p)$ of the big jumps is replaced by the set $D_m$, which for $m\ge1$ equals $\{T_p:p\in\mathcal T_m\}$. The display (8.27) drops the factor $1_{\{\Delta X_{T_p}\neq0\}}$ of the sentence before it; $\widetilde U(m)$ keeps it. $|x|^r$ in $H^n(m)$ uses $0^r=0$, also for $r=0$. Writing $A_0=E$ explicitly avoids Lean's $1/0=0$.
-- source:
--   Jacod, Todorov, Do price and volatility jump together?, arXiv:1010.4990v1 (Ann. Appl. Probab. 20 (2010)), §8.1, pp. 24–26 ((8.3), Ω_{n,t,m}, A_m, (8.5)); §8.2, pp. 26–28 (𝒢_m, 𝓕^(m), D_m, Ω(m, n, S, i)±); §8.4, pp. 33–34 ((8.25), (8.27), H^n(m))

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_JacodTodorov10_LLN_Scheme

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

namespace JacodTodorov10.LLN

/-- The **localized assumption (8.3)** (arXiv:1010.4990v1, §8.1, pp. 24–25), with constant `C`, one
process `Γ` and functions `γ`, `γ̂`:
* `γ`, `γ̂` are measurable and nonnegative, with `∫_E (γ^r ∧ 1) dλ < ∞` and
  `∫_E (γ̂^q ∧ 1) dλ < ∞`, `q = 2` if `v ≤ 1/2` and `q = 1/v` if `v > 1/2` ((H-r)(c), (8.2));
* `|δ| ≤ Γγ`, `|δ̂| ≤ Γγ̂`, and `Γ` plays `Γ'` in (2.2): `|Z̄_{t+s} − Z̄_t| ≤ Γ_{t+s} s^v` for
  `0 < s ≤ 1` ("we can always take the same process Γ_t … as we may do for the process Γ′", p. 24);
* for all `ω`, `t`, `z`: `σ_t ≠ 0` and
  `|b_t| + |σ_t| + 1/|σ_t| + |b̂_t| + |σ̂_t| + |σ̂'_t| + Γ_t + |Z_t| + |Z̄_t| + γ(z) + γ̂(z) ≤ C`.

The paper reduces every theorem of §3 to this case by localization (p. 24–25) and assumes it
throughout §8.

Formalization Note: the printed (8.3) also contains the term `|X_t|`. It is omitted here: together
with `|b_t| ≤ C` and `1/|σ_t| ≤ C` for all `t ≥ 0`, a bound `|X_t| ≤ C` for all `t` cannot hold
(for large `a`, `e^{aX_t}` would be a bounded process whose drift is bounded below by a positive
constant), so keeping it would make every statement under (8.3) vacuous. The localization of §8.1
modifies the coefficients after a stopping time and yields exactly the bounds kept here. -/
def Bdd83 {Ω E : Type*} [MeasurableSpace E] (lam : Measure E) (M : Data Ω E) (r v C : ℝ)
    (Γ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (γ γhat : E → ℝ) : Prop :=
  Measurable γ ∧ Measurable γhat ∧ (∀ z, 0 ≤ γ z) ∧ (∀ z, 0 ≤ γhat z) ∧
    ∫⁻ z, ENNReal.ofReal (min (pow0 (γ z) r) 1) ∂lam < ⊤ ∧
    ∫⁻ z, ENNReal.ofReal (min (pow0 (γhat z) (if v ≤ 1 / 2 then 2 else 1 / v)) 1) ∂lam < ⊤ ∧
    (∀ ω t z, |M.δ ω t z| ≤ Γ t ω * γ z) ∧ (∀ ω t z, |M.δhat ω t z| ≤ Γ t ω * γhat z) ∧
    (∀ ω (t s : ℝ≥0), 0 < s → s ≤ 1 →
      |M.Zbar (t + s) ω - M.Zbar t ω| ≤ Γ (t + s) ω * (s : ℝ) ^ v) ∧
    ∀ ω (t : ℝ≥0) (z : E), M.σ t ω ≠ 0 ∧
      |M.b t ω| + |M.σ t ω| + 1 / |M.σ t ω| + |M.bhat t ω| + |M.σhat t ω| + |M.σhat' t ω| +
        Γ t ω + |M.Z t ω| + |M.Zbar t ω| + γ z + γhat z ≤ C

/-- The set `A_m = {z : γ(z) ≤ 1/m}` (arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 25), with `A_0 = E` ("Note that
A_0 = E", p. 26). -/
def A {E : Type*} (γ : E → ℝ) (m : ℕ) : Set E :=
  if m = 0 then Set.univ else {z | γ z ≤ 1 / (m : ℝ)}

/-- The big-jump times at level `m`: the times `s` of the atoms `(s, z)` of `μ` with `z ∉ A_m`
(arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 27: `D_m = {(ω, s) : μ'^{(m)}(ω, {s} × E) = 1}`, with `μ'^{(m)}` the
restriction of `μ` to `ℝ₊ × (A_m)^c`). For `m ≥ 1` this is the set `{T_p : p ∈ 𝒯_m}` of p. 25. -/
def Dm {Ω E : Type*} (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (γ : E → ℝ) (m : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : Set ℝ≥0 :=
  {s | ∃ z, (s, z) ∈ N ω ∧ z ∉ A γ m}

/-- The σ-field `𝒢_m` generated by the measure `μ'^{(m)}`, the restriction of `μ` to
`ℝ₊ × (A_m)^c` (arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 26). -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def G {Ω E : Type*} [MeasurableSpace E] (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (γ : E → ℝ) (m : ℕ) :
    MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ (B : Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (_ : MeasurableSet B),
    MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => cnt N ω (B ∩ (Set.univ ×ˢ (A γ m)ᶜ))) inferInstance

/-- The filtration `(𝓕^{(m)}_t)`: the smallest filtration containing `(𝓕_t)` and such that
`𝓕^{(m)}_0` contains `𝒢_m`, i.e. `𝓕^{(m)}_t = 𝓕_t ∨ 𝒢_m` (arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 26). -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def Fm {Ω E : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] [MeasurableSpace E]
    (𝓕 : Filtration ℝ≥0 ‹MeasurableSpace Ω›) (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (γ : E → ℝ) (m : ℕ)
    (t : ℝ≥0) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  𝓕 t ⊔ G N γ m

/-- The set `Ω_{n,t,m}` of arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 25: any two distinct big-jump times `T_p ≠ T_q`
(`p, q ∈ 𝒯_m`) satisfy `T_p > t`, or `T_p > 3k_nΔ_n` and `|T_p − T_q| > 6k_nΔ_n`. The times are
taken from `Dm`, without the enumeration `(T_p)`. -/
def OmegaNTM {Ω E : Type*} (S : Scheme) (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (γ : E → ℝ) (n : ℕ) (t : ℝ≥0)
    (m : ℕ) : Set Ω :=
  {ω | ∀ s ∈ Dm N γ m ω, ∀ s' ∈ Dm N γ m ω, s ≠ s' →
    t < s ∨ ((3 * S.k n * S.Δ n : ℝ) < s ∧ (6 * S.k n * S.Δ n : ℝ) < |(s : ℝ) - s'|)}

/-- The set `Ω(m, n, S, i)_+ = {(i − 1)Δ_n < S ≤ iΔ_n, (S, S + (k_n + 1)Δ_n] ∩ D_m = ∅}` of
arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 28, for a random time `S` and a random integer `i`. -/
def OmegaPlus {Ω E : Type*} (Sc : Scheme) (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (γ : E → ℝ) (m n : ℕ)
    (S : Ω → ℝ≥0) (i : Ω → ℤ) : Set Ω :=
  {ω | ((i ω : ℝ) - 1) * Sc.Δ n < S ω ∧ (S ω : ℝ) ≤ i ω * Sc.Δ n ∧
    ∀ s ∈ Dm N γ m ω, ¬ ((S ω : ℝ) < s ∧ (s : ℝ) ≤ S ω + (Sc.k n + 1) * Sc.Δ n)}

/-- The set `Ω(m, n, S, i)_− = {(i − 1)Δ_n < S ≤ iΔ_n, (S − (k_n + 2)Δ_n, S) ∩ D_m = ∅}` of
arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 28. -/
def OmegaMinus {Ω E : Type*} (Sc : Scheme) (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (γ : E → ℝ) (m n : ℕ)
    (S : Ω → ℝ≥0) (i : Ω → ℤ) : Set Ω :=
  {ω | ((i ω : ℝ) - 1) * Sc.Δ n < S ω ∧ (S ω : ℝ) ≤ i ω * Sc.Δ n ∧
    ∀ s ∈ Dm N γ m ω, ¬ ((S ω : ℝ) - (Sc.k n + 2) * Sc.Δ n < s ∧ s < S ω)}

/-- The index `i(n, s) = ⌈s/Δ_n⌉`, the unique integer with `s ∈ ((i − 1)Δ_n, iΔ_n]` when `s > 0`
(arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 25, `i(n, p)`). -/
noncomputable def iOf (S : Scheme) (n : ℕ) (s : ℝ≥0) : ℤ :=
  ⌈(s : ℝ) / S.Δ n⌉

/-- The big-jump part `Ũ^n(m)_t` of (8.25) (arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 33):
`∑_{p ∈ 𝒯_m(n,t)} F(Δ^n_{i(n,p)} X, ĉ(k_n, p−), ĉ(k_n, p+)) 1_{|Δ^n_{i(n,p)} X| > u_n}`, where
`𝒯_m(n, t) = {p ∈ 𝒯_m : T_p ≤ Δ_n[t/Δ_n]}`, `ĉ(k_n, p−) = ĉ(k_n)_{i(n,p)−k_n−1}` and
`ĉ(k_n, p+) = ĉ(k_n)_{i(n,p)}` (p. 26). The sum runs over the big-jump times `s ∈ D_m`. -/
noncomputable def Utilde {Ω E : Type*} (S : Scheme) (X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ)
    (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (γ : E → ℝ) (F : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) (m n : ℕ) (t : ℝ≥0) (ω : Ω) :
    ℝ :=
  ∑ᶠ s ∈ {s : ℝ≥0 | s ∈ Dm N γ m ω ∧ (s : ℝ) ≤ S.Δ n * ⌊(t : ℝ) / S.Δ n⌋₊},
    F (S.incr X n (iOf S n s) ω) (S.chat X n (iOf S n s - S.k n - 1) ω)
        (S.chat X n (iOf S n s) ω) *
      (if S.u n < |S.incr X n (iOf S n s) ω| then 1 else 0)

/-- The limit `Ũ(m)_t` of (8.27) (arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 33):
`∑_{p ∈ 𝒯_m} F(ΔX_{T_p}, c_{T_p−}, c_{T_p}) 1_{ΔX_{T_p} ≠ 0} 1_{T_p ≤ t}`, a sum over the big-jump
times `s ∈ D_m` with `s ≤ t`. The factor `1_{ΔX_{T_p} ≠ 0}` is the one in the sentence before
(8.27); the display (8.27) drops it. -/
noncomputable def Ulim {Ω E : Type*} (X σ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E))
    (γ : E → ℝ) (F : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) (m : ℕ) (t : ℝ≥0) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  ∑ᶠ s ∈ {s : ℝ≥0 | s ∈ Dm N γ m ω ∧ s ≤ t},
    F (pjump X s ω) (cLeft σ s ω) (c σ s ω) * (if pjump X s ω ≠ 0 then 1 else 0)

/-- `Xpp` is the small-jump process `X''(m)` of (8.5) (arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 26):
`X''(m)_t = ∫_0^t ∫_{A_m} δ(s, z)(μ − ν)(ds, dz)` if `r > 1` (a compensated integral, `HasCompInt`
with integrand `δ 1_{A_m}`), and `X''(m)_t = ∫_0^t ∫_{A_m} δ(s, z) μ(ds, dz)` if `r ≤ 1`, the a.s.
absolutely convergent sum of `δ` over the atoms of `μ` in `[0, t] × A_m`. -/
def IsXpp {Ω E : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] [MeasurableSpace E] (P : Measure Ω)
    (lam : Measure E) (N : Ω → Set (ℝ≥0 × E)) (δ : Ω → ℝ≥0 → E → ℝ) (γ : E → ℝ) (r : ℝ)
    (m : ℕ) (Xpp : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  if 1 < r then HasCompInt P lam N (fun ω t z => (A γ m).indicator (fun z' => δ ω t z') z) Xpp
  else ∀ t : ℝ≥0, ∀ᵐ ω ∂P,
    Summable (fun p : {p : ℝ≥0 × E // p ∈ N ω ∧ p.1 ≤ t ∧ p.2 ∈ A γ m} => |δ ω p.1.1 p.1.2|) ∧
    Xpp t ω = ∑' p : {p : ℝ≥0 × E // p ∈ N ω ∧ p.1 ≤ t ∧ p.2 ∈ A γ m}, δ ω p.1.1 p.1.2

/-- `H^n(m)_t` of arXiv:1010.4990v1, p. 34, without its constant factor `K`:
`∑_{i = k_n+1}^{[t/Δ_n] − k_n} |Δ^n_i X''(m)|^r (1 + ĉ(k_n)_{i−k_n−1} + ĉ(k_n)_i)`, with
`|x|^0 = 1_{x ≠ 0}` (`pow0`). -/
noncomputable def Hn {Ω : Type*} (S : Scheme) (X Xpp : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (r : ℝ) (n : ℕ) (t : ℝ≥0)
    (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  ∑ i ∈ Finset.Icc (S.k n + 1) (⌊(t : ℝ) / S.Δ n⌋₊ - S.k n),
    pow0 |S.incr Xpp n i ω| r * (1 + S.chat X n ((i : ℤ) - S.k n - 1) ω + S.chat X n i ω)

end JacodTodorov10.LLN


